GS pipelining (plan P8). PS2X_GS_TIMING=1 now also reports the threaded backend's worker every 2 s ("[gs:worker]": idle time, time in batches and how it splits into run scanning, inline draws, banded runs with their setup, band 0 and wait, serial draws and the other commands, the draw counts, and each band's busy time), and "[gs:sync]" the commands still queued when the producer started to wait for a drain. Banding by area: every queued draw carries a conservative row range and the number of pixels the rasterizer walks (computed on the producer's thread); a run is banded when it has at least 24 draws or covers at least PS2X_GS_BAND_PIXELS pixels (default 4096), so a few big draws no longer run on one thread; the rows are split between the bands by estimated cost, not in equal parts; a band skips the draws that lie outside its rows (and a band with no rows does nothing but keep band 0's CLUT replay); the run-splitting checks are skipped for a draw whose relevant state equals the previous draw's. PS2X_GS_BAND_COST=0 restores the old rules (draw count only, equal rows). PS2X_GS_BANDS_VERIFY=1 still redraws every banded run serially and compares.

